---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Two-party contract (multi-sig) · enprot">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-3">Two-party contract (multi-sig)</h1>
  <p class="text-enprot-muted mb-6">
    Both parties must sign to advance. Pure multi-sig, no key distribution
    (each party already has their key).
  </p>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Scenario</h2>
    <p>
      A law firm and a client are negotiating an SLA. The contract evolves through
      multiple versions; both sides must agree to each change. The contract file itself
      must reflect every party's sign-off, and any party must be able to verify the
      other's signature on any past version.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Setup</h2>
    <pre class="bg-enprot-ink text-enprot-paper p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code># Each party generates their keypair independently
enprot keygen ed25519 --out-priv law.pem    --out-pub law.pub
enprot keygen ed25519 --out-priv client.pem --out-pub client.pub

# They exchange pubkeys (out of band — that's key distribution)
LAW_FP=$(enprot fingerprint law.pub)
CLIENT_FP=$(enprot fingerprint client.pub)</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Negotiation round</h2>
    <pre class="bg-enprot-ink text-enprot-paper p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code># Law firm drafts and signs their half of a new anchor
enprot encrypt --anchor --signer law.pem \
    -w Terms -k Terms=v3-draft contract.ept

# Client reviews, amends text, adds their signature to the SAME anchor
# (amend-only-the-signature operation; payload-hash unchanged)
enprot co-sign --signer client.pem contract.ept</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
      The anchor now has two signers. The <code>signer:</code> field lists both fingerprints;
      the <code>signature:</code> field carries two semicolon-separated signatures.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Verification under policy</h2>
    <pre class="bg-enprot-ink text-enprot-paper p-4 rounded overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>cat > .enprot/policy.toml &lt;&lt;EOF
[chain]
trust_roots = ["ed25519:$LAW_FP", "ed25519:$CLIENT_FP"]
required_signers = 2
EOF

enprot verify-chain --policy-file .enprot/policy.toml contract.ept</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
      <code>required_signers = 2</code> enforces that every anchor carries both parties'
      signatures. Single-signed anchors (one party tried to push a change unilaterally)
      fail verification.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Capability framing</h2>
    <table class="w-full border border-enprot-ink/10 text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-enprot-ink/5">
        <tr><th class="p-2 text-left">Participant</th><th class="p-2 text-left">Holds</th><th class="p-2 text-left">Capability</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="p-2">Law firm</td><td class="p-2">law.pem</td><td class="p-2 font-mono">Signer(law_fp)</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="p-2">Client</td><td class="p-2">client.pem</td><td class="p-2 font-mono">Signer(client_fp)</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="p-2">Either</td><td class="p-2">other's .pub</td><td class="p-2 font-mono">Verifier(other_fp)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm">
      Neither party can advance the contract alone. The policy file pins both fingerprints;
      enforcement is local to each party's verification.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Status</h2>
    <p>
      Specified in <a href="https://github.com/engyon/enprot/blob/main/TODO.finalize/28-contract-mode.md" class="text-enprot-accent hover:underline"><code>TODO.finalize/28</code></a>.
      Depends on Stage 1 + Stage 4a.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
